title: Schema file
tags: Schema
kind: reference
summary: The JSON format — groups of targets and constraints — where it is found, and what makes it invalid.

`.metafolder/schema.json`, unless the repository's `config.json` names another
file in its `schema` key (relative to `.metafolder/`, or absolute). With neither,
the repository has no schema and nothing is validated.

At `init`, the daemon seeds `.metafolder/schema.json` with a copy of the shipped
`~/.config/metafolder/daemon/schema.default.json`. That copy is a convenience: a
missing default is silently skipped and never fails `init` (an exception to
[[No runtime fallback]], since nothing is being read for the daemon's own use).

!! Format

|!Key |!Type |!Meaning |
|`version` |int |the format version, currently `1` |
|`groups` |list |constraint groups |

A group:

|!Key |!Type |!Meaning |
|`targets` |`"*"` or a list of type names |the types it applies to; `"*"` for every metarecord |
|`constraints` |list |the constraints each target gets |

A constraint:

|!Key |!Type |!Default |!Meaning |
|`field` |string |required |the constrained field |
|`type` |string |any |its value type ([[Value types]]): `nothing`, `string`, `int`, `float`, `bool`, `datetime`, `ref`, `tree_ref`, `refbase`, `externalref` |
|`min` |int |`0` |the fewest rows it may have |
|`max` |int |unlimited |the most rows it may have |
|`description` |string |— |free text, for a GUI to show |
|`default` |bare value |— |the value a client pre-fills a new metarecord of this type with |

`default` is a ''bare'' JSON value, read through the constraint's `type` — a
number for `int`, a string for `string`, `{"parent": …, "name": …}` for `tree_ref`
— so a constraint with a `default` must declare a `type`, and the value's kind must
match it. Leaving `default` out templates the field as `Nothing`. Like
`description`, it is informational: the daemon never writes it or validates with
it; it is returned as it is by `GET /schema`, which is where the GUI's type-aware
"new metarecord" reads its templates.

A type may be the target of several groups, and several constraints may bear on one
field of one type (global ones stack with per-type ones): all of them apply.

!! Loading

The file is read when the repository is loaded, and by `mf schema reload`. An
unreadable or invalid file — malformed JSON, an unknown value type, `min > max`,
`min < 0`, `targets` neither `"*"` nor a non-empty list of strings, a constrained
field with a reserved name (`mfr_*`, `mf_*`), a `default` without `type` or of
the wrong kind — makes the load fail with `400`, naming the offending constraint.
Loading the repository without validation instead would let violating writes
through: a broken schema is a configuration error to fix. A failed reload keeps
the previous schema.
